    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d22-a2">

                <pb facs="0083" n="33" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg33"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure A in inclosure 1 in No.
                    92.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >District Captain’s Office, in Mies</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1894-07-08"><hi rendition="#italic">July 8,
                                1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The contents of these acts having been shown to David Hofmann, he produced two
                    papers made out in English purporting to be proofs of his American citizenship.
                    Thereupon he was told that for reasons of public welfare and according to
                    paragraph 2 of the law of the 27th of July, 1871, he was to be expelled forever
                    from Austria, and that he must leave within eight days or be escorted over the
                    frontier under a guard.</p>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">salv. rex.</hi></p>
                <p>I take cognizance of the foregoing and request a copy of this sentence, wishing
                    to appeal against it.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">David Hofmann.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Certified to be a true copy.</p>
                    <p>Signature of the clerk of the court.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
